{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"D (they/them)","id":"692746345387130900","is_bot":0,"username":"nonbianarydarry"},"author_id":"692746345387130900","channel_id":"852737863170654259","content":"A spotlight appears at the top of the tent. Above your heads are two lythe, muscular elfish folk in costume. One is adorned in yellows and golds, the other in dark blues and silvers. Without warning they both leap off of their pedestals from the top of the tent and soar through the air, at the last moment catching bars strung from the ceiling. They swing over your heads at incredible speeds, contorting their bodies around various colored silks with ease. The singer, who remains unseen, sings a song in a language you don’t recognize. Although you don’t know what the lyrics are, you feel the meaning. She takes you through a journey of sadness and remorse, war and turmoil, justice and harmony. The two figures continue in tandem with the music until the story reaches its finish. All goes silent until an applause from the crowd erupts.","created_at":"2021-07-11T01:24:59.348000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"863591671941431326","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
